course: dictionary
lesson: 15518
title: Formal words: subsist
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Subsist is a formal word, so you will meet it in books, history lessons and exams. It means to stay alive, usually with very little food or money. «The shipwrecked sailors subsisted on coconuts and rainwater for three weeks.» The clues are shipwrecked, coconuts and rainwater: they were not eating a proper meal, they were just staying alive.
explain: Subsist can also mean to continue to exist. «An old custom still subsists in the village, even though few people remember why it began.» Nothing is being eaten here: the custom simply carries on. Try a plain word in the sentence, such as "an old custom still survives", and check that it still makes sense.
explain: The noun is subsistence. Subsistence farming means growing just enough food to feed your own family, with little left over to sell. «Many families subsisted by farming and fishing.» The clues are farming and fishing: they lived off the land and the sea.
fact: Subsist is a verb: I subsist, she subsists, they subsisted, subsisting.
fact: The noun is subsistence, as in subsistence farming.
fact: «Subsist» means to stay alive, often with very little food or money.
fact: «Subsist» can also mean to continue to exist.
fact: Plain words you can swap in are live on, survive and get by.
exercise: «The shipwrecked sailors subsisted on coconuts and rainwater.» What does subsisted mean here? | *Stayed alive on very little | Sailed quickly back home | Built a large boat | Ate a huge feast every night
exercise: Which word is the noun form of subsist? | subsisted | subsist | *subsistence | subsists
exercise: «An old custom still subsists in the village.» What does subsists mean? | It has been forgotten and buried | *It continues to exist | It is being sold at the market | It moves from place to place
test: «Lena's family subsisted by growing vegetables and keeping hens.» What does subsisted mean? | Moved to a new country | *Lived on what they grew and kept | Got rich from selling food | Forgot how to cook
test: Which plain word could replace subsist in «They subsisted on bread and water»? | Shout | *Get by | Forget | Explode
exam: «The old tradition still subsists, even after a hundred years.» What is the best meaning of subsists? | *It continues to exist | It has disappeared | It is shared with a neighbour | It is written down in a book
